---
title: Slow cooker honey mustard chicken thighs
servings: 6
course: dinner
tags: slow-cooked, chicken
image: https://images.immediate.co.uk/production/volatile/sites/30/2020/08/honey-mustard-chicken-f111be8.jpg?resize=440,400
source: https://www.bbcgoodfood.com/recipes/slow-cooker-honey-mustard-chicken-thighs
prep time: 5m
cook time: 4h20m
---

Heat the #slow cooker{}. Melt the @butter{1%tbsp} in a #frying pan{} and quickly brown the @chicken thigh{8}(or fillets if you prefer) all over. Make sure the skin picks up plenty of colour. Season, then put them in the #slow cooker{}. Brown the @spring onion{8}(cut into lengths) and add them to the #slow cooker{} as well. Add the @chicken stock{150%ml}, @dijon mustard{1%tbsp} and @honey{2%tbsp} and cook on low for ~{4%hours}.

Stir in the @double cream{2%tbsp} and @pea{100%g}(frozen), then cook for a further ~{15%minutes} with the #lid{} off. Re-crisp the chicken skin in the #air fryer{} at 200 C for ~{4%minutes}, if you like.
